m=A.mv("Nowadays, we need to find ways to make cleaning up and sorting trash easier in homes and factories. Using smart machines and robots can help us do this work without needing so many people. This is especially good for places where it might be dangerous for people to work. As our cities get increasingly crowded and we want to keep our environment clean, dealing with trash becomes even more challenging. That's why we need to come up with new ways to sort garbage automatically. In our project, we're trying to use computer vision - which is like giving computers eyes - and robots to help sort trash. We're using a real-time object detection algorithm namely YOLO (You Only Look Once) that can quickly spot different types of trash. This could help us deal with our trash problem better and keep our cities cleaner and healthier. By working on this, we hope to make a real difference in how Indonesia handles its trash. If we can make sorting trash easier and better, we can help reduce pollution, save resources, and make our country a nicer place to live for everyone.","images/trash-ai/logo.png","Trash AI",A.c(["images/trash-ai/trash-ai.png"],i),m,"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e_bFbAODZGiJoxWeYWkW8MoB8ezzsztyfcxiRMRlWOU/edit?usp=sharing")
